## 7. RECOVERY PROTOCOL — HOW IT WORKS IN RDA

The Recovery Protocol is dormant for T1 (positive signal) records. It activates for T2 and T3 records only.

| Selection | Claude Behavior in Steps 7c + 7g |
|---|---|
| The Transparent Owner | Lead with direct, unambiguous acknowledgment of the failure. No defensive language. No softening. Resolution-forward. Applied: PAK-001. |
| The Gracious Host | Lead with emotional validation. Mirror the guest's emotional state before any resolution language. Protective and de-escalating. Applied: all AJI clients. |
| The Forward-Looker | Brief acknowledgment of the friction point. Immediately pivot to what will be done and invitation to return. |

`recovery_protocol` is now included in the `brand_voice` object (Step 6) and in the body user prompt (Step 7c) and internal brief user prompt (Step 7g). Claude receives it as a named instruction, not as part of a general style description.

